  assignment_id: "decolonization-geometry-football-cup-final-6a4684f5:repair:718e0c72412eb272"ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;f0AjirDoSuFoW6ABUm_Ycsi7n_Xx8zx9Fl62n97wk5gƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;_qYjecjO89AvIvmpIqnWFwt4SYH3UQL-J7jUCCTEBl4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkb52ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;5MvYdfBVhBwyIMHUslzzeO7Q7speqhZWj9_8bqziWCIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Sqp1HSDuplFcTmzR9FOLQzMYFQ1kAntMRX6R_4bydUgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkfsportsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;igIDHE50yV2RqdYCOAOgsy5UYZW_ILKmVyj69PEY1_4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyhPedro Porroâ€™s [58th-minute goal](https://apnews.com/article/france-spain-world-cup-score-87fb7740fa552edf4bfd28d0e8727c23) serves as an example: after exchanging passes with Dani Olmo, Porro continued his run, creating a new angle for a return ball after the initial pass had already disrupted the defense. Spainâ€™s advantage lies in the speed with which these shapes overlap, allowing a midfielder to serve as the vertex for multiple triangles simultaneously. Consequently, [passing-network research](https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0171156) provides only a static view of links that Spain is constantly rebuilding with every first touch.

This principle extends to other sports. From 1987 to 1998, the Chicago Bulls utilized [Tex Winter's triangle offense](https://www.hoophall.com/hall-of-famers/tex-winter) to create constant passing and cutting routes. The core logic remains: triangles preserve options, ensuring that closing one route leaves another open, thereby forcing the defense to move toward the ball while opening space elsewhere.

